			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1485566">
									

<p>At first I didn't like this one all that much, but then I read what Gears said and I really started liking the idea that she's not a human child, she's some eldritch abomination from beyond the void that wears the disguise of a child and its mere presence is enough to drive us mad. This girl shaped 'thing' is so alien and beyond our scope of understanding that its very being drives us over the edge, we don't have to know what it is because what it is so incomprehensible that it breaks our minds. That's why we try to kill it, our brain doesn't know what's wrong, it can't know what's wrong but it knows it's the girl and it knows she needs to die right now before her presence destroys your mind.</p>
<p>That's why I like 053 now, not because she's an immortal brat but because she's a little girl who's not a little girl at all. Maybe the form of a little girl isn't what it looks like at all and it's just the closest thing our mind can comprehend (like the color magenta but instead of a color it's a physical impossibility beyond the constraints of sanity.)</p>

